      {
        "title": "Ben Shelton’s Pliable Ceiling",
        "url": "https://www.tennisabstract.com/blog/2026/11/17/ben-sheltons-pliable-ceiling/",
        "published_at": "Tue, 17 Nov 2026 11:50:51 +0000",
        "status": "read",
        "text_sha256": "52f9fcd6e4430bcb3bb8464b9fb5b8b4931b163cc54bac408deb67a34d870faf",
        "scope": "player_background",
        "excerpts": [
          "A few years ago I asked, What Is Ben Shelton’s Ceiling? A big serve can get you a long way in this sport. But without a return game to match, the margins are perilously thin. In 2023, Shelton won 32.7% of his return points. Only one player has ever posted a number so low and finished in the top ten: John Isner in 2018. Last year, Shelton won 33.3% of his return points. That stands as the second -lowest RPW% for a top-tenner, at least since 1991, the span for which those stats are available.",
          "Break points? The theory about guys like Sampras, Isner, and Nick Kyrgios is that they didn’t go full-out on all return points. So their RPW% doesn’t reflect their actual chances of breaking serve. Indeed, in 2023, Shelton won over 40% of his break point chances, breaking serve 18 more times than expected."
        ],
        "note": "读到 28 段",
        "match_verified": false
      }
    ],
